<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 428.3 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 428.3 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of December 19 raised 428.3 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 323.1 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 219.5 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.29 (14.36)	   40.4 (47.2)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.21 (16.36)	   43.6 (71.7)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.16 (17.36)	  122.0 (78.8)</p>
<p>    24 months		 20.04 (20.50)	  222.3 (125.4)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,552.25 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,552.75 a week earlier and 1,597 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
